  "scope": "Resolve Markdown note embeds through snapshot-bound VaultRoot and VaultSession APIs, filter non-Markdown targets, enforce depth/cycle guards before bounded source reads, validate selected subpaths, and keep vault reads stable against concurrent changes.",
  "behavior": [
    "VaultRoot::resolve_note_embed accepts only Embed references and an existing regular Markdown source note. Candidate resolution includes regular Markdown files only, so images and other attachments cannot enter the note-transclusion read path.",
    "The resolver applies the depth/cycle guard before opening a uniquely resolved target. It checks the snapshot size against the 512 KiB limit before opening, reads at most the bounded source, verifies the target hash against the captured entry, and re-snapshots before returning a result.",
    "Heading/block subpaths use the crates/doc source-preserving slice API. Duplicate basenames are inspected one candidate at a time and disambiguated by subpath outcomes; ambiguous, unresolved, external, invalid-UTF-8 and cycle/depth cases fail closed.",
    "Vault snapshots now hash regular files with a fixed 64 KiB buffer rather than retaining each complete file in memory."
  ],
